Third-party code

This product has ZERO third-party runtime dependencies. The trusted kernel
(cli/core/ and pwa/core/) uses only Node.js built-in modules and Web-native
APIs (Web Crypto, Web Streams). There is no npm runtime package, no CDN fetch,
no third-party WebAssembly, and no vendored third-party crypto/zip/pdf library.
The files under `pwa/vendor/` are first-party adapters written by the project
(SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT), not third-party libraries.

External services (not embedded code)

The optional, off-by-default "Aegis" hash-anchor toggle talks to a user-configured
endpoint over HTTP; it sends only a textual root hash, package id and spec version.
The optional, off-by-default external RFC3161 TSA mode sends only the textual root
hash to a user-configured endpoint; that endpoint may be a third party outside the
user's jurisdiction and the user is responsible for the transfer assessment.
Neither service changes the local-first, offline-by-default behavior. See
docs/EXTERNAL-TSA-DISCLOSURE.md.

Build-time / test tooling is not shipped in the runtime product:
  - Headless-Chrome browser checks (cli/test/ui-browser-check.mjs) — dev/test only
  - python3 -m http.server (local static serving) — local runtime tool, not a dependency

